Destination MAC address: 01:00:5e:01:01:01

Explanation:
The IPv4 multicast group used in the lab was 239.1.1.1. IPv4 multicast
addresses are mapped to Ethernet MAC addresses using the 01:00:5e prefix
and the lower 23 bits of the multicast IPv4 address. This produces
01:00:5e:01:01:01.

The value was confirmed in multicast.pcap. The capture contains five ICMP
Echo Requests from 10.10.10.1 to 239.1.1.1 with Ethernet destination
01:00:5e:01:01:01, followed by five ICMP Echo Replies from 10.10.10.2.
